{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host","id":137965,"title":"Setting Idea: Uratha as the Wolf Host.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T04:04:58-07:00","id":137965,"title":"Setting Idea: Uratha as the Wolf Host.","content":"As in, Uratha are Shartha.<br /> <br /> Each Werewolf has a scrap of Father Wolf grafted onto them by their first change; instead of consuming each-other, they follow the urge to come back together by forming packs and hunting.<br /> <br /> How much would this change things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T04:10:02-07:00","id":137974,"title":"","content":"Cool! Great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T04:14:55-07:00","id":137976,"title":"","content":"The idea was actually proposed in one of the supplements, can't remember which one off the top of my head though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T04:18:55-07:00","id":137978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=137976#post137976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea was actually proposed in one of the supplements, can't remember which one off the top of my head though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I'm just getting into Werewolf now (excited for Idigam), so that's interesting to hear.<br /> <br /> Do you remember if they fleshed the idea out? I mean, given the parallels between Uratha and Shartha by default, it isn't much of a leap to get one from the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T06:01:02-07:00","id":137995,"title":"","content":"Predators, perhaps some other books.<br /> In Predators it points out a theory that the shartha and the Uratha are related, since they have so many commonalities. But it also points out that none of the shartha are as 'developed' as the Uratha, with their forms, easy adaptation (becoming shartha tends to kill the mortal host) and gifts.<br /> <br /> It suggests the shartha are what werewolves could have been (or the other way around). But that's just another theory among the many we have.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T07:39:28-07:00","id":138045,"title":"","content":"It's, at the very least, strongly implied in Predators that if you have a huge, ancient Pangaean demon-god who dies, chances are it'll come back wearing lots and lots of human skins. Happened that way to Grandmother Spinner, the Plague King, the Famine-Bringer, the Carrion Prince, the Sea Serpent - and Father Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T08:54:52-07:00","id":138099,"title":"","content":"0.0 I love this idea, i don't know why I never thought of it myself. In retrospect it's so obvious. But it's so cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:03:49-07:00","id":138107,"title":"","content":"Well, the myth is that uratha killed father wolf, but maybe it's bakwards, and they did not cause his death, his death caused them, dividing his spirith into a hundred thousand shards. But then, who killed the ultimate predator?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/524-angrycucaracha","name":"AngryCucaracha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:22:03-07:00","id":138141,"title":"","content":"If you want to go further, there are some theories elsewhere and you could make vampires blood hosts, progeny of the Crone or Belial or Zmai (this is mentioned as one of the options to its history) or whomever you wanted, Sin-Eaters are more like ghost-claimed than anything else but you could have geists be shards of the original spirit of death, and mages as hosts of the universe (or perhaps its creator), what with how their arcana vaguely correlate to influence of broad themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-15-2014, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:57:57-07:00","id":138167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AngryCucaracha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=138107#post138107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the myth is that uratha killed father wolf, but maybe it's bakwards, and they did not cause his death, his death caused them, dividing his spirith into a hundred thousand shards. But then, who killed the ultimate predator?</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the firstborn who became the totems of the Uratha tribes killed Father Wolf. They were not werewolves, they were wolf spirits. The Uratha (and the Pure for that matter) did not exist until after Father Wolf's death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:06:08-07:00","id":138175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=138141#post138141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to go further, there are some theories elsewhere and you could make vampires blood hosts, progeny of the Crone or Belial or Zmai (this is mentioned as one of the options to its history) or whomever you wanted, Sin-Eaters are more like ghost-claimed than anything else but you could have geists be shards of the original spirit of death, and mages as hosts of the universe (or perhaps its creator), what with how their arcana vaguely correlate to influence of broad themes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting. I would actually make the Strix the spirit shards of some sort of shadow or owl spirit, and vampires their human host bodies. Diablerie sure takes on a new meaning then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:06:59-07:00","id":138176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=138167#post138167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, the firstborn who became the totems of the Uratha tribes killed Father Wolf. They were not werewolves, they were wolf spirits. The Uratha (and the Pure for that matter) did not exist until after Father Wolf's death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think you got that backwards. The Uratha, also known as the First Pack, did kill Father Wolf. After his death, the Uratha were not powerful enough to take up his duty, and sought out the Firstborn (the totem spirits, children of Father Wolf and other wolf spirits) and made them tribal totems by earning their patronage. The Uratha hunted with Father Wolf, as well, and were definitely (as far as myths can be definite) alive before they murdered him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:14:15-07:00","id":138182,"title":"","content":"The part of the myth that states that, as the werewolf race expanded and flourished, Father Wolf got progressively weaker and weaker, lends further credence to the entire Host theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:16:47-07:00","id":138185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=138176#post138176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Think you got that backwards. The Uratha, also known as the First Pack, did kill Father Wolf. After his death, the Uratha were not powerful enough to take up his duty, and sought out the Firstborn (the totem spirits, children of Father Wolf and other wolf spirits) and made them tribal totems by earning their patronage. The Uratha hunted with Father Wolf, as well, and were definitely (as far as myths can be definite) alive before they murdered him</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh... Weird, I definitely misread something, then. I still prefer my version and will continue using it in my werewolf games, but I prefer to be aware of the default fluff and make changes consciously and intentionally. Thank you very much for pointing that out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:22:39-07:00","id":138191,"title":"","content":"(Insert random noone ever reads the books rant here)<br /> <br /> It's kinda really, truly, seriously important to the mythology of the Forsaken that it was THEM who killed the Father. Not some spirit. You. The core mythology is about making hard, tough choices that will only hurt you in the end, but that still are the right choices. Having the Firstborn, not the Forsaken, be the ones who killed Father Wolf kinda diminishes this major, quintessential theme of the game quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:31:27-07:00","id":138195,"title":"","content":"Again I point out that there appears to be in-universe confusion between the First Pack and the Firstborn and that the Uratha of the tribes are the adoptive/spiritual children of the Firstborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:37:09-07:00","id":138208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=138191#post138191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Insert random noone ever reads the books rant here) It's kinda really, truly, seriously important to the mythology of the Forsaken that it was THEM who killed the Father. Not some spirit. You. The core mythology is about making hard, tough choices that will only hurt you in the end, but that still are the right choices. Having the Firstborn, not the Forsaken, be the ones who killed Father Wolf kinda diminishes this major, quintessential theme of the game quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, whether it was the firstborn or the Uratha who killed father wolf, it was not you personally unless you're playing a game set immediately after his death (which actually might be kind of interesting, but that's beside the point). Whether it was your biological ancestors who killed him or not is questionable, since it is just a myth anyway. At any rate, my own version of the story is still all about those themes of making the right choices in spite of them hurting you and those you care about. I just changed some of the details but keep the core message the same. Admittedly, I'm disappointed with myself that I inadvertently made those changes without the specific intention of deviating from the fluff as written. I did read the book, but I misunderstood it, I guess. Nonetheless, I agree with you that those are essential themes of Forsaken and despite my misunderstanding I ended up with a version that does very much preserve those themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:38:37-07:00","id":138211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=138182#post138182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part of the myth that states that, as the werewolf race expanded and flourished, Father Wolf got progressively weaker and weaker, lends further credence to the entire Host theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I particularly like that bit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:44:56-07:00","id":138216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137965-setting-idea-uratha-as-the-wolf-host?p=138195#post138195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I point out that there appears to be in-universe confusion between the First Pack and the Firstborn and that the Uratha of the tribes are the adoptive/spiritual children of the Firstborn.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yup, that would be where I got thrown off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T11:09:37-07:00","id":138258,"title":"","content":"You know what might be cool?<br /> <br /> A Chronicle where one of the other Hosts (I'm thinking Spiders, just because tank-sized spiders with bone sword-legs are <i>awesome</i>) gets that little... extra that the Uratha have. They get the smooth shapeshifting, the survival of the host, everything.<br /> <br /> As you might imagine, this would cause quite the uproar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T11:45:11-07:00","id":138302,"title":"","content":"Then you'd get those spider bastards from apocalypse, only more pissed off at werewolves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attac